<title>USA: Continental wanted merger to head off American - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Continental wanted merger to head off American - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Airlines last summer approached its rival Delta Air Lines about a merger partly as a pre-emptive strike to keep American Airlines from becoming a global powerhouse that could overrun midsized carriers such as Continental, The Wall Street Journal reported Thursday.</p>
<p>The pitch was to beat American to the punch before it merges its trans-Atlantic operation with British Airways or moves to acquire U.S. Air Group Inc, as some industry experts expect.</p>
</text>
